  'tour.welcome.b': 'This short tour walks you around the playmat. Your side is at the <b>bottom</b>, Gary’s side is at the <b>top</b>, and the panel on the right is where you choose your moves and get coaching.<br><br>You can replay this tour any time with the <b>Tutorial</b> button at the top.',
  'tour.active.t': 'Your Active Pokémon',
  'tour.active.b': 'This is the Pokémon that is fighting right now. <b>Only the Active Pokémon can attack</b>, and it is the one that takes the opponent’s attacks.<ul><li>The bar and number under the card show its remaining <b>HP</b>.</li><li>Dice on the card are <b>damage counters</b>: each pip or number is 10 damage.</li><li>Energy cards tucked under it are what pays for its attacks.</li></ul>Hover any card to read it up close.',
  'tour.bench.t': 'Your Bench',
  'tour.bench.b': 'Up to <b>5 Pokémon</b> wait here. Benched Pokémon:<ul><li>can receive Energy and evolve, getting ready to fight,</li><li>step into the Active Spot when your Active Pokémon is Knocked Out or retreats.</li></ul>If your Active Pokémon is Knocked Out and your Bench is empty, you lose, so keep some Pokémon here.',
  'tour.hand.t': 'Your hand',
  'tour.hand.b': 'These are your cards. You see them, Gary does not. There are three kinds:<ul><li><b>Pokémon</b>: Basic ones go to the Bench, Stage 1 and Stage 2 evolve a Pokémon already in play.</li><li><b>Energy</b>: attach <b>one per turn</b> to a Pokémon.</li><li><b>Trainers</b>: one-time effects like healing or drawing cards.</li></ul>Greyed-out cards can’t be played right now. Hover one to see why.',
  'tour.prizes.t': 'Prize cards',
  'tour.prizes.b': 'At the start, the top <b>6 cards</b> of your deck are set aside face down. Each time you <b>Knock Out</b> one of Gary’s Pokémon, you take one into your hand.<br><br><b>Take all 6 and you win.</b> Gary has its own Prize cards at the top right.',
  'tour.piles.t': 'Deck and discard pile',
  'tour.piles.b': '<b>Deck</b>: you draw 1 card from it at the start of every turn. If you have to draw and it is empty, you lose.<br><b>Discard pile</b>: used Trainers, discarded Energy and Knocked Out Pokémon go here. The number shows how many cards are in each pile.',
  'tour.opp.t': 'Gary’s side',
  'tour.opp.b': 'This is a mirror of your side: Gary’s Prize cards, Active Pokémon, Bench, deck and discard pile. Your attacks hit <b>Gary’s Active Pokémon</b> (the one closest to the middle).<br><br>Every decision on this side is made by <b>Gary</b>, an AI trainer powered by Kev, a decision model running locally on your computer.',
  'tour.midbar.t': 'Turn bar',
  'tour.midbar.b': 'Shows <b>whose turn it is</b> and the turn number, how many cards Gary holds, what Gary just decided (and how sure it was), and the <b>win meter</b>: the Professor’s estimate of your chances of winning.',
  'tour.moves.t': 'Your move',
  'tour.moves.b': 'Every move you are allowed to make right now is listed here, grouped by type (Attack, Energy, Evolve, Bench, Trainer cards, Retreat). Click one to do it.<ul><li>The tip at the top says what matters right now; open the rest with <b>more tips</b>.</li><li>The <b>Professor</b> rates every move: the percentage and the thin line under it show how good it looks, and the best one is labelled <b>Professor’s pick</b>.</li><li><b>Attacking ends your turn</b>, so do your other moves first. <b>End turn</b> is always at the bottom, and it glows when nothing useful is left.</li><li>Under it, the <b>Professor</b> comments on your last move.</li></ul>',
  'tour.viewer.t': 'Card preview',
  'tour.viewer.b': 'Hover over any card on the table, in your hand or in a choice window, and a large preview pops up next to it, with an explanation in your language of what it does: HP, Weakness, attacks and when to use it.<br><br>For greyed-out cards in your hand, a red note in the preview explains why you can’t play them yet.',
  'tour.coach.t': 'Settings',
  'tour.coach.b': 'The gear button opens <b>Settings</b>:<ul><li>The Professor: turn move ratings and suggestions on or off,</li><li>turn coin, dice and attack animations on or off,</li><li>choose <b>pip</b> or <b>numbered</b> damage dice.</li></ul>Your choices are remembered.',
  'tour.log.t': 'Game log',
  'tour.log.b': 'Everything that happens is written here: draws, attacks, coin flips, damage and Knock Outs. The yellow <b>rule notes</b> explain each rule the first time it comes up, so you learn while you play.',
  'tour.firstTurn.t': 'How a turn works',
  'tour.firstTurn.b': '<ol><li>You <b>draw</b> a card automatically.</li><li>Put <b>Basic Pokémon</b> from your hand on your Bench.</li><li><b>Evolve</b> Pokémon if you can (not on the first turn of the game).</li><li><b>Attach one Energy</b> to a Pokémon, usually your Active one.</li><li>Play helpful <b>Trainer</b> cards.</li><li><b>Attack</b> if your Active Pokémon has enough Energy. Otherwise click <b>End turn</b>.</li></ol>The player who goes first cannot attack on turn 1. Good luck, Trainer!',
