  // ---- Rule notes ----
  'rule.mulligan': "Mulligan: your opening hand must contain a Basic Pokémon. If it doesn't, you reshuffle and draw again, and your opponent may draw 1 extra card for each mulligan.",
  'rule.setup': 'Setup: each player puts 1 Basic Pokémon face down as their Active Pokémon and may put up to 5 more on the Bench.',
  'rule.prizes': 'Prize cards: each player sets aside the top {n} cards of their deck face down. Each time you Knock Out an opposing Pokémon you take 1 into your hand. Take them all to win!',
  'rule.draw': "Every turn starts by drawing a card. If your deck is empty and you can't draw, you lose!",
  'rule.firstTurn': "The player who goes first can't attack on their very first turn.",
  'rule.bench': 'Benching: you can play Basic Pokémon to your Bench (max 5) at any time during your turn. They are your backups and your evolution targets.',
  'rule.evolve': "Evolution: put a Stage 1 card on the matching Basic, or a Stage 2 on the matching Stage 1. The Pokémon keeps its damage and Energy, and Special Conditions are removed. You can't evolve on either player's first turn, or evolve a Pokémon the same turn it was played.",
  'rule.energy': 'Energy: you may attach only ONE Energy card per turn. Attacks need specific Energy, and the Colorless (star) symbol can be paid with any type.',
  'rule.trainerModern': 'Trainer cards today: Items (any number each turn), Supporters (1 per turn), Stadiums (1 per turn, it stays in play) and Pokémon Tools (stay attached). A used Item or Supporter goes to the discard pile.',
  'rule.trainer': 'Trainer cards: in the Base Set era you could play as many Trainers as you liked each turn. Each one goes to the discard pile after use (except PlusPower and Defender, which stay attached for a while).',
  'rule.retreat': "Retreat: once per turn you may swap your Active Pokémon with a Benched one by discarding Energy equal to its Retreat Cost. Asleep or Paralyzed Pokémon can't retreat.",
  'rule.energyRemoval': "Energy Removal slows your opponent down by taking away Energy they've already attached. It's one of the strongest cards in the Base Set.",
  'rule.tool': 'PlusPower adds 10 damage to an attack this turn. Defender reduces damage taken by 20 until the end of the opponent\'s next turn.',
  'rule.status.poisoned': 'Poisoned: put 1 damage counter (10 damage) on it between every turn. It is cured by evolving or moving to the Bench.',
  'rule.status.asleep': "Asleep: it can't attack or retreat. Between turns its owner flips a coin, and heads wakes it up.",
  'rule.status.paralyzed': "Paralyzed: it can't attack or retreat during its owner's next turn. After that it recovers.",
  'rule.status.confused': 'Confused: when it attacks, flip a coin. Tails means the attack fails and it takes 30 damage. Retreating or evolving cures it.',
  'rule.weakness': '{m} is weak to {t}, so the damage was doubled! Check the Weakness box at the bottom of a card before you attack.',
  'rule.resistance': 'Resistance: damage from the type shown is reduced by 30.',
  'rule.prevent': 'Some attacks, like Withdraw, Stiffen and Harden, prevent damage during the next turn. Sometimes the right move is to wait or use a different attacker.',
  'rule.ko': "Knock Out: when a Pokémon's damage reaches its HP it is Knocked Out and discarded with everything attached, and the opponent takes a Prize card. Take all {n} to win!",
  'rule.checkup': 'Pokémon Checkup happens between turns: Poison deals damage, Asleep Pokémon flip to see if they wake up, and Paralysis wears off.',

